#
# What a sale is worth, in Sutra: bottles * price, the price per bottle in
# integer minor units of the books' currency (cents for USD). Bottles and
# price fit 9(9), so a larger or a negative one is a size error: refused,
# never cut short. sale.cpp says the same in C++ (as WebAssembly), which
# answers to 64 bits: past nine digits the two disagree and it is held.
record vintner-sale
  bottles: 9(9)
  price: 9(9)
  worth: 9(18)
procedure
  compute worth = bottles * price
  answer worth
